<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ælla of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 867</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ælla (died 867) was king of Northumbria in the 860s, having displaced King Osberht. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a> seized York in 866, the rival kings made peace and attacked the city together in March 867, but both were killed. Later Norse sagas made Ælla the slayer of the legendary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> Ragnar Lodbrok and told of his gruesome death at the hands of Ragnar's sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aella-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="Ælla of Northumbria" width="320" height="252" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugo Hamilton (1802–1871) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ragnar_Lodbroks_d%C3%B6d_by_Hugo_Hamilton.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
